86521055 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521404 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "9d3f167d-1c36-5660-a850-11a37b74e56b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521424 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186520770 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521424 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186520855 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521424 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186520952 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521424 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186521126 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521424 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186521312 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521424 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521424 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521424 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186520770 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521424 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "be2e5806-e4f1-5967-90f4-2ffdb0fd7652" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521465 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186521424 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521465 #edb/ref 1069 "q-53700" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521465 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521465 #edb/ref 1071 "Write the equation of the parabola $y=-2{x}^{2}-8x-14$ in vertex form." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521465 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1b44bc96-863e-5a73-a2ed-628d5188e295" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521465 #edb/ref 1074 "To express the equation of the parabola in vertex form, we need to complete the square. \n\nFirst, we take out a factor of $-2$ from the entire expression:\n\n$$\n-2{x}^{2}-8x-14=-2({x}^{2}+4x+7)\n$$\n\nNow, we complete the square for the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+4x+7 & = \\\\ {x}^{2}+2\\cdot 2\\cdot x+7 & = \\\\ {x}^{2}+2\\cdot 2\\cdot x+{2}^{2}-{2}^{2}+7 & = \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 2\\cdot x+{2}^{2})-{2}^{2}+7 & = \\\\ (x+2)^{2}-{2}^{2}+7 & = \\\\ (x+2)^{2}-4+7 & = \\\\ (x+2)^{2}+3 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute this result back into our original expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2({x}^{2}+4x+7) & = \\\\ -2((x+2)^{2}+3) & = \\\\ -2(x+2)^{2}-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, expressed in vertex form, the equation of the parabola is $y=-2(x+2)^{2}-6.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521482 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186521404 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521482 #edb/ref 1069 "q-13411" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521482 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521482 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the equation of the parabola whose vertex is $(-5,4)$ and leading coefficient is $2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521482 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "39734cdd-98b1-5bc5-a3ba-0e209592784a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521482 #edb/ref 1074 "Remember that the vertex form of a parabola is\n\n$$\ny=a(x-h)^{2}+k,\n$$\n\nwhere $(h,k)$ are the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola, and $a$ is the leading coefficient.\n\nSubstituting $(h,k)=(-5,4)$ and $a=2$ into the above and then expanding and simplifying, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2(x-(-5))^{2}+4 \\\\  & =2(x+5)^{2}+4 \\\\  & =2({x}^{2}+10x+25)+4 \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}+20x+50+4 \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}+20x+54.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is $y=2{x}^{2}+20x+54.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521541 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186521392 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521541 #edb/ref 1069 "q-106267" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521541 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521541 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the equation of the parabola whose vertex is at $(-8,-20)$ and whose leading coefficient is $1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521541 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b1cfb6c9-bb07-5ff5-8e41-4388a89b7e12" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521541 #edb/ref 1074 "Remember that the vertex form of a parabola is\n\n$$\ny=a(x-h)^{2}+k,\n$$\n\nwhere $(h,k)$ are the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola, and $a$ is the leading coefficient.\n\nSubstituting $(h,k)=(-8,-20)$ and $a=1$ into the above and then expanding and simplifying, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =1(x-(-8))^{2}-20 \\\\  & =(x+8)^{2}-20 \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+16x+64-20 \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+16x+44.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is $y={x}^{2}+16x+44.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521577 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "11ddce49-fc64-55d5-b99d-ac3a1e4e7463" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521577 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186521541 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521636 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186521655 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521636 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b6cc5e9a-8556-5a56-8111-da471df13050" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521636 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186521482 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521655 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186521577 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521655 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f5d9c43c-614d-5288-9746-7f31a2326b3e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521655 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186521465 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
